# ==============================================================================
# HMS Automated Backup Schedule Configuration (crontab template)
# ==============================================================================
# IMPORTANT POLICY NOTE (G-09 / OD-06):
# The permanent backup schedule and retention duration REQUIRE OWNER APPROVAL.
# These entries are configurable templates. Do not activate in production without
# owner sign-off.
#
# PENDING OWNER DECISIONS:
# 1. Full Backup Frequency: Daily at 02:00 UTC vs Twice Daily (02:00 & 14:00 UTC).
# 2. Retention Duration: 30 days vs 90 days vs 7 years (tax/financial compliance).
# 3. Off-site S3 Sync: Immediate after backup vs Batch sync window.
# ==============================================================================

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin
HMS_ENV_FILE=/path/to/hms/.env

# Proposed Schedule Option A (Daily Full + Continuous WAL for 15-min RPO):
# At 02:00 UTC every day, run full encrypted database and object storage backup.
# (PostgreSQL continuous WAL archiving runs independently via archive_command).
0 2 * * * /path/to/hms/infrastructure/scripts/backup.sh >> /var/backups/hms/cron.log 2>&1

# Proposed Schedule Option B (High-Activity: Every 6 hours):
# 0 */6 * * * /path/to/hms/infrastructure/scripts/backup.sh >> /var/backups/hms/cron.log 2>&1

# Optional Weekly Archive Drill (Dry-run integrity validation every Sunday at 04:00 UTC):
# 0 4 * * 0 /path/to/hms/infrastructure/scripts/dr-prepare.sh >> /var/backups/hms/dr_preflight.log 2>&1
